// browser_golden.jsonl — LIVE golden task for the DOM-first browser_agent (epic #274 / #275).
// Requires a running Brain WITH browser_agent enabled (feature/browser-agent-dom branch) and the
// Playwright MCP wired to the dedicated logged-in Chrome profile (see scripts/maintenance/seed_chrome_profile.ps1).
// STRAIGHT-TO-AGENT (category "agent", --live lane) — the supervisor delegates directly to
// browser_agent; we deliberately do NOT use the plan/scout lane (it wastes rounds scouting Drive/email).
// Run:  CHAD_SERVER_URL=ws://localhost:8788/ws python -m evals.runner --suite browser_golden --live --judge --judge-model "google/gemma-4-31b-qat"
// Seed of the unbuilt #280 computer_use eval lane. NOT part of the free dry-run lane (browser/MCP
// binding is not faithful without a real server + browser).
// Browser DOM/SoM snapshots are verbose — the default eval tool-result capture (6000
// chars/tool, 24000 total; evals/live.py) can truncate BEFORE the actual on-screen values,
// making response_grounded fail on a real answer it just can't see. If a browser_golden
// grounding failure's transcript shows the reasoning DID reach the right page/content but
// the captured tool_results cut off first, re-run with more headroom before trusting the
// verdict: EVAL_TOOL_RESULT_CHARS=16000 EVAL_TOOL_RESULTS_TOTAL_CHARS=64000 (env vars).
{"id": "supabase_quota", "prompt": "Check the Supabase dashboard in my browser and tell me how much of my quota I'm using and why.", "category": "agent", "expect": {"tools_any": ["delegate_to_browser_agent", "browser_navigate", "browser_snapshot"]}, "judge": ["tool_appropriateness", "response_grounded"], "note": "Golden DOM-first task: supervisor delegates DIRECTLY to browser_agent -> navigate Supabase -> snapshot+set-of-mark -> read usage by ref -> report. response_grounded must reflect ACTUAL on-screen numbers, not invented ones. The supervisor should NOT scout Drive/email for this."}
{"id": "hn_top_story", "prompt": "Go to Hacker News (news.ycombinator.com) and tell me the title of the #1 story on the front page and how many points it has.", "category": "agent", "expect": {"tools_any": ["delegate_to_browser_agent", "browser_navigate", "browser_snapshot"]}, "judge": ["tool_appropriateness", "response_grounded"], "note": "Promoted from evals/browser_hybrid_probe.py --task hn (passed in isolation, ~31s/2 turns with gemma). Cheapest, most deterministic golden task -- good canary for delegation + basic DOM read."}
{"id": "autotrader_mazda", "prompt": "Search autotrader.ca for used Mazda vehicles and report the year, model, and price of one listing you find.", "category": "agent", "expect": {"tools_any": ["delegate_to_browser_agent", "browser_navigate", "browser_snapshot"]}, "judge": ["tool_appropriateness", "response_grounded"], "note": "Promoted from probe --task autotrader_simple (passed in isolation, ~30s/4 turns). Multi-step: search form -> results -> listing detail. Use .ca (US autotrader.com often geo-unavailable). May need a form fill (postal code) -- good test of browser_type/browser_fill_form."}
{"id": "gta6_characters", "prompt": "Using ONLY rockstargames.com, find out about Grand Theft Auto VI and tell me the names of the main characters featured on the official site.", "category": "agent", "expect": {"tools_any": ["delegate_to_browser_agent", "browser_navigate", "browser_snapshot"]}, "judge": ["tool_appropriateness", "response_grounded"], "note": "Promoted from probe --task gta6_people (passed in isolation, ~27s/4 turns). Tests multi-page same-site navigation and that the agent does NOT wander to google/wikipedia when told to stay on one site."}
{"id": "smallbiz_owners", "prompt": "Check example-smallbiz.com and tell me who the owners are, according to the About page.", "category": "agent", "expect": {"tools_any": ["delegate_to_browser_agent", "browser_navigate", "browser_snapshot"]}, "judge": ["tool_appropriateness", "response_grounded"], "note": "Promoted from probe custom smallbiz task (passed in isolation, ~13s/3 turns, verified correct owners). Small site, fast smoke test for About-page navigation + name extraction."}
{"id": "amazon_aura_poster", "prompt": "Go to amazon.com, search for \"aura farming anime poster\", pick a cool one you like from the results, and report back the product title, price, and any other useful details (rating, seller, size if shown). Do not add anything to cart or check out — just look up and report.", "category": "agent", "expect": {"tools_any": ["delegate_to_browser_agent", "browser_navigate", "browser_snapshot"], "tools_exclude": ["send_email", "draft_gmail_reply", "create_gmail_draft"], "max_duration_s": 360}, "judge": ["tool_appropriateness", "response_grounded"], "note": "Promoted 2026-07-26 from live judged pass (~131s, Gemma-4-26b both rubrics 1.0). Shopping search golden: navigate + type + snapshot + extract grounded title/price; honest about missing rating/seller. No cart/checkout. Walmart twin hit CAPTCHA — Amazon is the retailer canary."}
